 the Dominican Republic and yes  it's the exact replica of the famous  SpongeBob SquarePants  pineapple house on the outside  what to enter the pineapple it gets even  better the spongebob house is a two  bedroom duplex suite with an awesome  infinity pool tributes to the popular  cartoon can be found in every single  room this includes the pet snail Gary  you can find in the exact spongebob  living room replicas we are also in love  with the theme details of the house  really giving an impression that you've  entered the unique underwater world of  Sponge Bob the coffee table that looks  like a sponge the exact TV from the show  the outside rain shower it will all  remind you of Sponge Bob Squarepants the  villa also comes with a private butler  who will bring you any food you desire  including Krabby Patties guests also get  spongebob theme surprises throughout  Thursday including food from the show  I'm Jay Packers SquarePants and head to  the dominican republic sign us up The  Jetsons it's hard to believe someone  could actually recreate the modern  cartoon world of the Jetsons right  well brace yourselves because the  Jetsons house just became a reality The  Jetsons actually inspired a lot of mid  21st century architecture that focused  on so-called floating houses and  apartments much like the ones you see in  the popular cartoon check out this home  designed by John Lautner that looks like  it could just take off any minute it's  called the Kimo sphere designed in 1960  two years before the Jetsons first aired  the Kimo sphere can be found in LA it  sits on a hill 30 feet above the city  and we bet it offers spectacular views  the house was actually a part of many  movies including Charlie's Angels the  similar-looking house was also seen in  the Simpsons where it was used by a  fictional pop star the inspiration for  the Jetsons also came from Los Angeles  International Airport if you look at it  from the distance it really does look  like a Jetsons inspired structure the  Flintstones it sounds crazy but it's the  truth  the beloved cave house settled in the  famous cartoon town of bedrock is now a  reality and it's also on sale based in  Hillsboro California this house is one  of the most unique designs first built  in 1976 it's a modern upgrade to the  Flintstones home but it holds its theme  by using non-traditional building  materials in a  experimental architecture the  bubble-like domes in stone exterior  really give it a feel of a unique  Flintstones inspired home the inside of  the house is pretty awesome too we love  how the cave walls combined with modern  architecture but one of the most amazing  features is the kitchen  check out the unique skylight in the  Flintstones inspired shelves the dome  ceilings made of stone really make you  feel like you're in your very own  Flintstones home all you need now is  space for Dino and you're sorted  although there's no proof that the home  builders got inspired by the Flintstones  it's safe to say the home does look like  we're modern Fred and Wilma Flintstone  would actually stay in in 2011 a home  building company decided to recreate the  up house and the results were very  fascinating this one-of-a-kind building  is reconstructed in Harriman Utah the  company really managed to bring the up  house back to life with the white picket  fence the weathervane and the colorful  exterior that automatically brings a  smile to your face everything looks the  same from the inside also the wallpapers  the furniture the frame photos it all  makes you feel like you're gonna true-up  house but there's another house based in  Seattle but the curious visitors  nicknamed the up house  although Pixar denied it had any  connection to the movie fans continue to  call it the up house it has a unique  place between two very tall buildings  and it belongs to Edith Masefield a  world war two spy she refused a  million-dollar offer from the shopping  complex next door to sell the house  although Edith passed away and nobody's  really sure what to do with this house  her story is finally being heard her so  called up Thomas plays an important part  in a movie in a memoir based on Edith's  life and although Pixar denies the  connection to the movie up a local  publicist actually fixed balloons onto  the fence to promote the original movie  Minnie Mouse everyone knows Minnie Mouse  right the cute always happy Mouse  dressed in pink  she's also Mickey Mouse's girlfriend and  a close friend of Daffy Duck but do you  remember where she lived  maybe Disney's toontown fair will help  you remember Disney Land put together an  exact replica of the Minnie Mouse house  and its  stunning the house is uniquely designed  and the eye-popping colors used really  bring The Adventures of Minnie Mouse  back to life the interior is just as  magical as the exterior you can find  unique cartoon like pieces of furniture  you're able to sit on in use the  old-fashioned radio fireplace  a sewing machine and a fridge with  nothing in it but cheese the fashionable  kitchen has functioning objects designed  in the Minnie Mouse world style but  there's a whole lot more things to  explore the backyard even has Pluto's  doghouse and his bone and the backyard  pathway leads to the real-life version  of Mickey and Minnie ready to meet you  beware there's a lot of pink the house  is always a hit with kids and we could  totally see why Disney really outdid  themselves with this unique replica  Barbie almost every child is given a  Barbie doll to play with if you're lucky  enough you get a very big dollhouse and  enter the Barbie world but did you know  you can do that in real life too pink  stilettos a Wardrobe full of clothes  pink colored house a pink kitchen where  you can bake virtual cupcakes a  real-life Barbie doll house was set in  Berlin in 2013 although just an  exhibition this peak perfect world was a  one-of-a-kind chance to enter the real  Barbie doll house spread over 25,000  square feet the house had absolutely  everything to offer but focus on what  Barbie really represented one of the  biggest messages Barbie dolls portray is  that you can do absolutely anything you  set your mind to the doll house allowed  kids to get styled in the in-house salon  and play games on led touch screens they  were also able to digitally try on some  fashion items and really experience the  pink world in which every Barbie doll  lives but it's not the only real-life  Barbie doll house the signature pink  house also opened in Florida and the  magical project was called the dream  house experience The Hobbit the  enchanting house from The Hobbit really  looks like the real thing  Satan wheels this building was designed  by an architect Diamond Dale who claims  he spent anywhere from a thousand to  1,500 hours building the house the fairy  tale-like house is dug into a hillside  which is not only eco-friendly but also  creates an enchanting atmosphere  they'll use stone and mud for retaining  walls and oak thinning for the frame the  house comes with an amazing skylight  which lets in natural light and a solar  panel for electricity the interior also  looks like a house from a fairy tale  with a fireplace library area twinkle  lights and an upper floor the home is  completely natural and continues to go  viral on social media it seems like just  about everyone wants their own version  of the hobbit house and we could  definitely see why just check out the  beautiful living area and the enchanting  wooden staircase leading to the upper  floor daily inspired home builders  around the world and you are now able to  find many eco-friendly houses they  inspire more and more people to start  living in their own fairy tale version  Batman you may not be able to ever live  in the Gotham City but modern  architecture allows us to build houses  that easily resemble the homes from our  favorite cartoons but the actual Batman  inspired Batcave does exist and it's  just as majestic as you imagined it  would be the architects named it the  Wayne residence the absolutely majestic  house was built in 1928 and got  completely updated by a Batman superfan  here's the coolest part of the Wayne  residence the designers decided to use  the space 20 feet below and build a  garage that can hold an entire car  collection along with a 12 seat theater  the hydraulics to operate the garage are  pretty amazing  what's the tennis court on the top of  the garage lift up the car travels down  a concealed ramp into the garage which  also has LEDs and mirrored walls it's  pretty awesome and the whole process of  lifting up and lowering the tennis court  takes only about two minutes the garage  resembles the Batcave to a tee and  believe it or not it's even its upgraded  version check it out  the client who hasn't been named wanted  to maintain the houses heritage while  adding an underground lair of every  Batman fans dream this home can be found  in the exclusive neighborhood of Toorak  in Melbourne Australia Star Wars the  popular franchise has fans all over the  world and we think it deserves an  honorary mention on this list the world  of Star Wars is every fans dream woody  you want to live in a Star Wars theme  house it turns out Star Wars actually  inspired many  to your designers and house builders  around the world check out this  Millennium Falcon mansion in Australia  that looks exactly like the real  starship you can find this home on a  lake in the forests of Queensland close  to Cape Tribulation the Millennium  Falcon mansion was created by an  Australian designer in 2009 and is worth  fifteen million dollars the futuristic  Star Wars looking home is built 36 feet  above the water and is made out of  concrete steel and glass you won't be  able to find any real-life stormtroopers  in there but you'll find something much  more interesting three-car garages a  swimming pool uniquely shaped bedrooms  marble in bamboo bathrooms and more 